# ---- Martha's conversation ----
dialogue.harvest_feast_host.off_season.text = The feast's over for this year, and the table's packed away.\nCome back when the fields are in.
dialogue.harvest_feast_host.meet_arrival.text = You walked all that way on an empty stomach, I can tell.\nI'm Martha. When the fields are in I cook for whoever turns up, and the bread comes first. We'll start you on <b>wheat</b>.
dialogue.harvest_feast_host.meet_arrival.opt.hail = Pleased to meet you, Martha.
dialogue.harvest_feast_host.first_words.text = Mind the table, it's longer than it looks.\nEvery year when the fields are in, I set it up here in the <color is="#ffd97a">Forgotten Temple</color> and feed whoever turns up. There's a lot of cooking between now and the feast. You look like you could carry a sack of flour.
dialogue.harvest_feast_host.first_words.opt.hail = Happy to help.
dialogue.harvest_feast_host.board_fresh.text = Board's up. Fields or kitchen, it all needs doing, and every job pays <msg key="harvestfeast.progression.currency.harvest_feast_coins.name"/> to spend at my shop.
dialogue.harvest_feast_host.board_fresh.opt.later = Later.
dialogue.harvest_feast_host.board_fresh_friendly.text = Wipe your boots. I saved you a chair.\nThere's an extra job on the board with your name on it.
dialogue.harvest_feast_host.board_fresh_honored.text = Oh good, it's you. Take your pick off the board before the others get to it.
dialogue.harvest_feast_host.board_fresh_revered.text = Sit. Eat something first, you look half starved.\nThe board will keep.
dialogue.harvest_feast_host.menu.text = Mind the pot. What can I do for you?
dialogue.harvest_feast_host.wheat_offer.text = Bread first. It always is.\nWild <b>wheat</b> grows on the <b>plains of the Emerald Wilds</b>. Pick me a good armful by hand and bring it back here.
dialogue.harvest_feast_host.wheat_offer.opt.accept = I'll bring wheat.
dialogue.harvest_feast_host.wheat_brief.text = Wild <b>wheat</b> grows on the <b>plains of the Emerald Wilds</b>. Pick it by hand and bring it to me here in the temple.
dialogue.harvest_feast_host.wheat_ready.text = That's a fine armful. The flour will be ground by morning.\nNow, a feast needs a roast. Come back when you're ready to go hunting.
dialogue.harvest_feast_host.wheat_ready.opt.turnin = Here's the wheat.
dialogue.harvest_feast_host.turkeys_offer.text = <b>Wild Turkeys</b> are out by day all over the <b>Emerald Wilds</b>, in the woods and on the plains. Fat and loud, and not as daft as they look.\nHunt a few, then come back to me. If they give you trouble, ask Bram the Shepherd.
dialogue.harvest_feast_host.turkeys_offer.opt.accept = I'll go hunting.
dialogue.harvest_feast_host.turkeys_brief.text = Hunt <b>Wild Turkeys</b> by day in the <b>woods</b> and on the <b>plains</b> of the Emerald Wilds, then come back to me.
dialogue.harvest_feast_host.turkeys_ready.text = You smell like the woods. Good, that means it went well.\nHere's the <b>pumpkin pie recipe</b> for the next job, with some <b>dough</b> and <b>spice</b> to start you off. And hold still: if you're going to chase turkeys all week, you might as well look like one.
dialogue.harvest_feast_host.turkeys_ready.opt.turnin = Back from the hunt.
dialogue.harvest_feast_host.pie_offer.text = Your turn at the stove. Use that <b>recipe</b> to learn it, then bake a <b>pumpkin pie</b> at a <b>Chef's Stove</b> from dough, a pumpkin and spice.\nYou've got the dough and spice from me. Pick a <b>pumpkin</b> in the <b>autumn woods</b> of the Emerald Wilds. For more dough, ask Tomas the Miller, and Elsie the Weaver knows where spice comes from.
dialogue.harvest_feast_host.pie_offer.opt.accept = I'll bake you a pie.
dialogue.harvest_feast_host.pie_brief.text = Bake a <b>pumpkin pie</b> at a <b>Chef's Stove</b> from dough, a pumpkin and spice. <b>Pumpkins</b> grow in the <b>autumn woods</b>. Tomas the Miller knows dough, and Elsie the Weaver knows spice.
dialogue.harvest_feast_host.pie_ready.text = Smell that. That's a pie somebody cared about.\nYou've done your share and more. Come and sit down; it's time we ate.
dialogue.harvest_feast_host.pie_ready.opt.turnin = Here's the pie.
dialogue.harvest_feast_host.feast_offer.text = Once a year we put it all on the table and eat till nobody can stand.\nBake a <b>pumpkin pie</b> at a <b>Chef's Stove</b>, cook some <b>meat</b> on a <b>Campfire</b>, and pick <b>carrots</b> in the <b>forests</b> of the Emerald Wilds. Bring it all here and we'll set it out together.
dialogue.harvest_feast_host.feast_offer.opt.accept = Let's set the table.
dialogue.harvest_feast_host.feast_brief.text = A <b>pumpkin pie</b> from a <b>Chef's Stove</b>, <b>cooked meat</b> from a <b>Campfire</b> and <b>carrots</b> from the <b>forests</b>. Then we eat.
dialogue.harvest_feast_host.feast_ready.text = Pie, roast and carrots. Now that's a feast.\nSit, eat, and take this home: a turkey that won't run off, with the year on it.\nThere's more here than we'll ever eat, though. Collect your share, then talk to me again. I've one last job for you.
dialogue.harvest_feast_host.feast_ready.opt.turnin = Here's everything.
dialogue.harvest_feast_host.feast_done.text = Still full? So am I, and so is everyone you took a plate to.\nThat's my story done till next year's feast, but the table stays set until it's over. There's <b>work</b> every day and <b>turkeys</b> whenever you want them. Tomas, Elsie and Bram have a <b>job</b> each too. Keep helping and my <b>shop</b> opens up. What can I do for you?
dialogue.harvest_feast_host.deliveries_offer.text = Look at all that's left. I won't see good food wasted.\nTomas, Elsie and Bram worked all week and never sat down. Take <b>Tomas</b> a <b>pumpkin pie</b>, <b>Elsie</b> a <b>roast vegetable</b> and <b>Bram</b> some <b>cooked meat</b>. The leftovers I gave you will do. They're about the <b>temple</b>.
dialogue.harvest_feast_host.deliveries_offer.opt.accept = I'll take them round.
dialogue.harvest_feast_host.deliveries_brief.text = A <b>pumpkin pie</b> for <b>Tomas</b> where the road meets the kweebec village, a <b>roast vegetable</b> for <b>Elsie</b> on the village's far side, and <b>cooked meat</b> for <b>Bram</b> on the meadow by the road in.\nOut of leftovers? Bake a pie at a <b>Chef's Stove</b> or cook on a <b>Campfire</b>.
dialogue.harvest_feast_host.daily_turkeys_offer.text = Yesterday's roast went down to the last bone. Hunt a few more <b>Wild Turkeys</b> in the <b>Emerald Wilds</b> and I'll start another.
dialogue.harvest_feast_host.daily_turkeys_offer.opt.accept = I'll go hunting.
dialogue.harvest_feast_host.daily_wheat_offer.text = Every loaf I baked today is already gone. Pick more <b>wheat</b> on the <b>plains</b>, or there's no bread in the morning.
dialogue.harvest_feast_host.daily_wheat_offer.opt.accept = I'll bring wheat.
dialogue.harvest_feast_host.daily_roast_offer.text = Cook some raw <b>meat</b> on a <b>Campfire</b> and bring it here. People keep eating it before it gets to the table.
dialogue.harvest_feast_host.daily_roast_offer.opt.accept = I'll bring a roast.
dialogue.harvest_feast_host.roast_brief.text = Any raw <b>meat</b> will do. Cook it on a <b>Campfire</b> and bring it here before somebody eats it.
dialogue.harvest_feast_host.extra_turkeys_ready.text = More turkeys? I'll never say no.\nThat's another roast for the table, and here's the <b>wishbone</b>. Take it to <b>Bram</b>; he knows what it's for. Ask me what needs doing whenever you want more.
dialogue.harvest_feast_host.extra_turkeys_ready.opt.turnin = More turkeys for you.
dialogue.harvest_feast_host.ready_generic.text = Let me see what you've brought.
dialogue.harvest_feast_host.ready_generic.opt.turnin = It's done.
dialogue.harvest_feast_host.who_are_you.text = Nobody important. I cook.\nWhen the fields are in, I come here, set out the long table and feed whoever turns up. Some years that's a dozen people. Some years it's everyone for miles.
dialogue.harvest_feast_host.about_feast.text = It's a thank-you, mostly. The fields gave us plenty, and the least we can do is eat it together.\nYou bring something, you take something home. That's all the rules there are.
dialogue.harvest_feast_host.opt.returned = I'm back.
dialogue.harvest_feast_host.opt.quests = What needs doing?
dialogue.harvest_feast_host.opt.shop = Let's see your shop.
dialogue.harvest_feast_host.opt.standing = How do we stand?
dialogue.harvest_feast_host.opt.almanac = Show me the Almanac.
dialogue.harvest_feast_host.opt.who = Who are you?
dialogue.harvest_feast_host.opt.feast = What's the feast for?
dialogue.harvest_feast_host.opt.back = Something else.
dialogue.harvest_feast_host.opt.farewell = See you at the table.

# ---- The shared meal and the invitation tour ----
quest.harvest_feast_shared_meal.title = Shared Meal
quest.harvest_feast_shared_meal.flavor = Nobody eats alone at my table. Roast a vegetable on a Campfire, bring it here, and sit down a while.
quest.harvest_feast_invitations.title = The Guest List
quest.harvest_feast_invitations.flavor = A long table's no good half empty. Talk to people around the Forgotten Temple and invite them to the feast, then come and tell me who's coming.
objective.harvest_feast.invite = Invite {0} people to the feast
dialogue.harvest_feast_host.meal_offer.text = Nobody eats alone at my table.\nRoast a <b>vegetable</b> on a <b>Campfire</b> and bring it here, and we'll share it. Come by every day if you like. There's always a chair.
dialogue.harvest_feast_host.meal_offer.opt.accept = I'll bring something.
dialogue.harvest_feast_host.meal_brief.text = Any <b>vegetable</b> will do: a carrot, corn, a pumpkin or a mushroom. Roast it on a <b>Campfire</b> and bring it to the table.
dialogue.harvest_feast_host.meal_ready.text = Sit, sit. Pass that here and have some of mine.\nThere. Now you've eaten properly today.
dialogue.harvest_feast_host.meal_ready.opt.turnin = Let's share it.
dialogue.harvest_feast_host.invitations_offer.text = A long table's no good half empty.\nGo and tell folk about the feast, anybody who'll stop for a word. <b>Invite a few people</b>, then come back and tell me who's coming.
dialogue.harvest_feast_host.invitations_offer.opt.accept = I'll spread the word.
dialogue.harvest_feast_host.invitations_brief.text = Talk to folk, anybody but me, and <b>invite them to the feast</b>. Start with the ones about the temple; they've worked all week and nobody's asked them yet. Come back once you've asked a few.
dialogue.harvest_feast_host.invitations_ready.text = That many? I'd best bake more bread.\nThank you. A full table's the whole point.
dialogue.harvest_feast_host.invitations_ready.opt.turnin = They're coming.
dialogue.harvest_feast_invitation.opt.invite = Come and eat with us at Martha's table.

# ---- The feast's villagers: Tomas the Miller, Elsie the Weaver and Bram the Shepherd ----
dialogue.harvest_feast_miller.off_season.text = The feast's packed away, and so's the flour.\nI'll be back with more when the fields come in next year.
dialogue.harvest_feast_miller.off_season.opt.farewell = Until next year, then.
dialogue.harvest_feast_miller.greeting.text = Don't stand too close, the flour gets on everything.\nI've hauled sacks up from the mill all week so the ovens never go cold. I could do with a seat at the long table once the feast gets going.
dialogue.harvest_feast_miller.mill.text = Down by the river, same as ever. The wheel turns whether I'm there or not.\nThis time of year every sack it grinds goes to the feast.
dialogue.harvest_feast_miller.dough.text = Flour first. Grind <b>wheat</b> into <b>flour</b> at a <b>Chef's Stove</b>.\nThen mix the flour with <b>eggs</b> and a <b>tankard of water</b> at the same stove, and that's your dough. Bram knows where to find eggs.
dialogue.harvest_feast_miller.opt.dough = How do I make dough?
dialogue.harvest_feast_miller.opt.mill = Where's your mill?
dialogue.harvest_feast_miller.opt.thanks = Thanks, Tomas.
dialogue.harvest_feast_miller.opt.back = Fair enough.
dialogue.harvest_feast_miller.opt.farewell = I'll let you get back to it.
dialogue.harvest_feast_miller.supper.text = Is that pumpkin pie? For me?\nStill warm, and she remembered I like the crust. Tell Martha I'll be first at the table next year, and I'll bring the flour.
dialogue.harvest_feast_miller.supper.opt.give = Martha sent you supper.
dialogue.harvest_feast_miller.flour_offer.text = The ovens eat flour faster than my mill can grind it.\nGrind <b>wheat</b> into <b>flour</b> at a <b>Chef's Stove</b> and bring me some. Wild wheat grows on the <b>plains of the Emerald Wilds</b>.
dialogue.harvest_feast_miller.flour_offer.opt.accept = I'll bring you flour.
dialogue.harvest_feast_miller.flour_offer.opt.later = Not today.
dialogue.harvest_feast_miller.flour_brief.text = Pick <b>wheat</b> on the <b>plains of the Emerald Wilds</b>, grind it into <b>flour</b> at a <b>Chef's Stove</b>, and bring the flour back here to me.
dialogue.harvest_feast_miller.flour_ready.text = Fine as dust. That's proper flour.\nThe ovens won't go cold tonight. Thanks.
dialogue.harvest_feast_miller.flour_ready.opt.turnin = Here's your flour.
dialogue.harvest_feast_weaver.off_season.text = The feast is over and the cloths are folded away.\nCome and find me when the fields are in again. I will have new ones by then.
dialogue.harvest_feast_weaver.off_season.opt.farewell = I'll look out for them.
dialogue.harvest_feast_weaver.greeting.text = I have been at my loom since dawn. It is good to stand somewhere else for a change.\nI wove the cloths for the long table. It would be nice to sit down at the feast and eat off one of them for once.
dialogue.harvest_feast_weaver.cloth.text = A runner for the middle of the table, wheat gold with an orange edge.\nSomebody always spills gravy on it, so I weave a new one every year.
dialogue.harvest_feast_weaver.spice.text = You make <b>Spices</b> at a <b>Chef's Stove</b>, from <b>flowers</b> and a <b>vegetable</b>.\nOr pick <b>pumpkins</b> by hand in the <b>autumn woods</b>. Every so often there is some spice beside one. I do not know why, and I do not ask.
dialogue.harvest_feast_weaver.opt.spice = Where do I get spice?
dialogue.harvest_feast_weaver.opt.cloth = What are you weaving now?
dialogue.harvest_feast_weaver.opt.thanks = Thank you, Elsie.
dialogue.harvest_feast_weaver.opt.back = It's lovely work.
dialogue.harvest_feast_weaver.opt.farewell = I won't keep you.
dialogue.harvest_feast_weaver.supper.text = Is that a roast vegetable? For me?\nMartha always notices who has not sat down. Thank you. I will eat it at the loom, and I will try not to spill any on the cloth.
dialogue.harvest_feast_weaver.supper.opt.give = Martha saved you some supper.
dialogue.harvest_feast_weaver.spices_offer.text = I need a little spice to dye the orange edge of the table runner. Martha takes whatever I do not use.\nMake <b>Spices</b> at a <b>Chef's Stove</b> from <b>flowers</b> and a <b>vegetable</b>, and bring them to me.
dialogue.harvest_feast_weaver.spices_offer.opt.accept = I'll make you some.
dialogue.harvest_feast_weaver.spices_offer.opt.later = Not today.
dialogue.harvest_feast_weaver.spices_brief.text = Make <b>Spices</b> at a <b>Chef's Stove</b> from <b>flowers</b> and a <b>vegetable</b>, then bring them here. Picking <b>pumpkins</b> in the <b>autumn woods</b> turns up some spice as well.
dialogue.harvest_feast_weaver.spices_ready.text = That is a good color. The runner will be the right orange this year.\nThank you. Martha will want what is left.
dialogue.harvest_feast_weaver.spices_ready.opt.turnin = Here are your spices.
dialogue.harvest_feast_shepherd.off_season.text = Feast's done. I'm off back up the hill before the sheep wander any further.
dialogue.harvest_feast_shepherd.off_season.opt.farewell = Safe walk home.
dialogue.harvest_feast_shepherd.greeting.text = Came down from the hills with fleece for the weaver. The sheep can look after themselves for a few days.\nThey can't, really. But I wasn't going to miss the feast.
dialogue.harvest_feast_shepherd.sheep.text = My sister. She says she doesn't mind.\nThat means I'm taking her back a whole pie.
dialogue.harvest_feast_shepherd.turkeys.text = <b>Wild Turkeys</b> only come out by day. Look in the <b>woods</b> and out on the <b>plains</b>. They spook easy, so a bow helps.\nEggs come from <b>chickens</b>, not turkeys. And feed a turkey some <b>corn</b> and it's yours, though a tame one won't give you anything.
dialogue.harvest_feast_shepherd.opt.turkeys = Any tips for turkeys?
dialogue.harvest_feast_shepherd.opt.sheep = Who's watching your sheep?
dialogue.harvest_feast_shepherd.opt.thanks = Thanks, Bram.
dialogue.harvest_feast_shepherd.opt.back = She's earned it.
dialogue.harvest_feast_shepherd.opt.farewell = Enjoy the feast.
dialogue.harvest_feast_shepherd.supper.text = That meat for me? Martha's doing, I bet.\nProper food. I've lived on bread all week. Tell her thanks, and don't tell my sister.
dialogue.harvest_feast_shepherd.supper.opt.give = Martha sent you supper.
dialogue.harvest_feast_shepherd.eggs_offer.text = Tomas wants eggs for his dough, and I'm the one who knows chickens. Lucky me.\nBring me some <b>eggs</b>. Chickens only lay in a <b>Chicken Coop</b>, so catch a few in a <b>Capture Crate</b> and house them.
dialogue.harvest_feast_shepherd.eggs_offer.opt.accept = I'll bring you eggs.
dialogue.harvest_feast_shepherd.eggs_offer.opt.later = Not today.
dialogue.harvest_feast_shepherd.eggs_brief.text = <b>Eggs</b> come from <b>chickens</b> in a <b>Chicken Coop</b>. Catch chickens in a <b>Capture Crate</b>, house them in the coop, and bring me what they lay.
dialogue.harvest_feast_shepherd.eggs_ready.text = Not one cracked. Good.\nTomas will be happy. Makes a change.
dialogue.harvest_feast_shepherd.eggs_ready.opt.turnin = Here are the eggs.
dialogue.harvest_feast_shepherd.opt.graveyard = Tell me about the Turkey Graveyard.
dialogue.harvest_feast_shepherd.graveyard.text = Every turkey the feast eats leaves its soul behind. They end up in a <b>graveyard</b> I know, and they don't rest. Neither does the big one.\nBring me a <b>Wishbone</b> and I'll take you and your party in. Martha gives you one each time you hand her <b>Extra Turkeys</b>. Put the souls down, then the <b>Great Turkey</b>. They'll settle after that.
dialogue.harvest_feast_shepherd.graveyard.opt.enter = Take me to the Turkey Graveyard. (costs a Wishbone, from Extra Turkeys)
dialogue.harvest_feast_shepherd.graveyard.opt.back = Maybe later.

# ---- The Turkey Graveyard: the dungeon Bram opens, its fight and the Great Turkey's Claim ----
# The graveyard's confirm screen and lines read these. Banners and notices print markup as text, so none of
# those values carries any; the defeat line's {0} is the player's share of the fight in whole percent and
# {1} how many seconds it took.
dungeon.harvest_feast_turkey_graveyard.name = The Turkey Graveyard
dungeon.harvest_feast_turkey_graveyard.description = The souls of the feast's hunted turkeys linger here, and the Great Turkey with them. Set them free. Bring friends.
dungeon.harvest_feast_turkey_graveyard.goal = Put down the waves of Turkey Souls around the fountain to wake the Great Turkey, then defeat it to set every soul free. Deal with the souls that come to its side, or they wear you down.
dungeon.harvest_feast_turkey_graveyard.cost_hint = Martha gives you a Wishbone each time you hand in Extra Turkeys. Ask her what needs doing.
dungeon.harvest_feast_turkey_graveyard.confirm = Snap the Wishbone
dungeon.harvest_feast_turkey_graveyard.chest = Your reward waits in the chest where it fell.
notify.harvest_feast_turkey_souls_rise = Turkey Souls rise from the graves!
notify.harvest_feast_turkey_souls_rise.sub = Wave {0}. Put them all down to wake the Great Turkey.
notify.harvest_feast_great_turkey_engaged = The Great Turkey rises!
notify.harvest_feast_great_turkey_engaged.sub = Put it down and every soul here goes free.
notify.harvest_feast_great_turkey_souls = More Turkey Souls come to its side!
notify.harvest_feast_great_turkey_flock = The Great Turkey gobbles, and the flock answers!
notify.harvest_feast_great_turkey_fury = The Great Turkey is furious!
notify.harvest_feast_great_turkey_defeated = The Great Turkey falls, and the souls go free!
notify.harvest_feast_great_turkey_defeated.sub = Your share: {0}%, in {1, number} seconds.
notify.harvest_feast_great_turkey_wiped = The Great Turkey struts on.
notify.harvest_feast_great_turkey_wiped.sub = Put the Turkey Souls down as they come to its side, or they wear you down.
claim.harvest_feast_great_turkey_chase = Great Turkey: Boss Kill
